WEBVTT

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:12.820
He--he made it?!

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:15.580
General Hyou actually reached Ri Boku?

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:19.460
Yeah. Y'gotta hand it to General Hyou!

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:22.080
Those instinctive-general's eyes of his

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:23.340
saw right through Ri Boku's maneuver!

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:25.340
saw right through Ri Boku's maneuver!

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:25.420
"Ri"

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:29.800
Now, then--I'll just be taking your head.

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:03.510
The Ultimate Instinctive Type

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:03.140
Ri Boku, sir, move to the back.

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:08.770
I never thought anyone would be able
to see through my Ryuudou flow.

00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:13.150
And to make it all the way here
on intuition alone? Inconceivable.

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:18.530
"Sho"

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:16.200
Not even Sho's celebrated
instinctive Kei Sha

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:18.990
ever perceived it in its entirety.

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:22.410
But you, Lord Hyou...

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:25.170
You seem to exist beyond my understanding:

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:28.840
the ultimate instinctive type of general.

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:30.340
You have my respect.

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:34.630
That's one thing I don't care for, Ri Boku:

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:38.850
"Hyou" "Chin"

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:38.850
your calm demeanor as you find
yourself backed into a corner.

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:47.310
Here I thought I'd strike your back
as you cleverly struggle and escape,

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:49.770
but apparently not.

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:53.320
Though that face says
you haven't given up, either.

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:59.240
Don't tell me you're thinking
of besting me in a duel.

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:04.750
Well, Shin? Is it over?

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:08.420
Hell, it ain't even started!

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:11.210
What are you doin', General Hyou?

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:18.890
Lord Hyou, I have never
unsheathed my sword.

00:03:18.890 --> 00:03:22.640
I fight my battles strictly
through ingenuity.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:26.430
Oh? Then there's even more up your sleeve?

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:33.820
There's a reason the flow ends here.

00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:35.280
A flag?

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:36.700
And it's getting closer.

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:47.330
What's wrong, Shin?

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:50.750
What the--

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:53.420
Something... something's there!

00:03:57.510 --> 00:03:59.930
You did well to see through my Ryuudou.

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:03.760
Unfortunately, however...

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:08.940
<i>...you </i>will be the one dying here.

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:18.110
"Hi"

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:20.030
Bi Hei! What is it?

00:04:20.030 --> 00:04:22.870
Did something happen to General Hyou?!

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:28.040
Ho--

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:29.210
Hou Ken!

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:38.130
Well, aren't <i>we </i>ominous.
And just who <i>are </i>you?

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:46.810
--Look out! The horses!
--Whoa there!

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:52.100
I am host to a savage god lurking within.

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:56.230
I am the only one who causes
even the heavens fear.

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:58.240
An act of God:

00:04:59.690 --> 00:05:03.570
I am Hou Ken, god of war.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:06.580
Wh-What?!

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:07.540
Hou Ken?

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:09.120
Did he say "Hou Ken"?

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:12.670
Then he's one of Sho's Three Greats...

00:05:12.670 --> 00:05:16.170
From back in Bayou--the man who--

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:19.010
Ah, so it's you:

00:05:19.010 --> 00:05:21.130
the fool who slayed Ou Ki.

00:05:25.010 --> 00:05:28.850
Aha. Now that I've met you,
I finally understand

00:05:28.850 --> 00:05:31.890
how that man could have lost.

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:35.060
There's not even the faintest
whiff of general about you.

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:40.190
Yet this oddity--this <i>other</i>--
positively stinks of war.

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:43.610
If you managed to take down
a genius like Ou Ki...

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:46.200
This must be one unprecedented battlefield

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:49.290
if they brought in an outsider like you.

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:50.830
Isn't that right, Ri Boku?

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:56.130
Very well.

00:05:56.130 --> 00:05:59.920
If this fellow here is to
be your very last blade,

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:01.840
I'll gladly shatter him.

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:04.840
I owe Ou Ki that much.

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:06.680
Lord Hyou, sir!

00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:10.390
And while I do <i>that</i>, <i>you </i>take down Ri Boku!

00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:12.020
Wh-<i>What</i>?!

00:06:12.020 --> 00:06:12.890
Understood!

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:13.730
Here they come!

00:06:13.730 --> 00:06:15.730
Protect Ri Boku!

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:18.650
<i>Now </i>we're picking up steam!

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:22.440
I am Lord Hyou.

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:25.990
If you even <i>have </i>a heart, engrave that--

00:06:25.990 --> 00:06:28.030
I have no need of your name.

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:33.910
I shall only judge whether
thou art genuine.

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:36.170
Then here goes, boy.

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:39.380
What--Hou Ken?!

00:06:39.380 --> 00:06:40.960
Is it really him?

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:42.880
Yeah--no doubt about it.

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:44.260
Hou Ken!

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:47.590
Hou Ken--now, of all times!

00:06:47.590 --> 00:06:49.930
What with the huge foe
that's the coalition army,

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:52.220
he'd totally slipped my mind!

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:55.640
Still, it's no wonder that he'd be here.

00:06:55.640 --> 00:06:59.480
After all, he was the commanding
general in Bayou!

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:00.480
Bayou?

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:05.070
General Hyou...

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:07.860
Get the hell outta my way!

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:29.140
He went flying--horse and all!

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:37.640
I knew you'd be capable
of this much, at least!

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:45.110
Lord Hyou!

00:07:48.110 --> 00:07:50.410
Th-The great Lord Hyou...

00:07:50.410 --> 00:07:52.280
In such a one-sided battle...

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:58.120
What is this?
Naught of thee resounds in me.

00:07:59.670 --> 00:08:01.880
You don't say.

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:05.510
I haven't been able to pick up
on anything from you yet, either.

00:08:05.510 --> 00:08:09.010
Hence the trouble I'm having--

00:08:09.010 --> 00:08:13.350
finding the right place to light the fire.

00:08:13.350 --> 00:08:18.600
Under the current conditions,
that place no longer exists.

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:22.860
My Ryuudou flow will keep your
troops circling for a while yet.

00:08:22.860 --> 00:08:28.110
Therefore, your reinforcements
will not be arriving.

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:33.660
You saw the trick and made it to the
center, but with only a few dozen horses.

00:08:33.660 --> 00:08:35.580
Or, to take the opposite point of view,

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:40.330
you went out of your way
to be completely surrounded.

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:45.420
And what you found there was Hou Ken,
an overwhelming martial force.

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:50.220
You've been losing momentum
for a while now, Lord Hyou--

00:08:50.220 --> 00:08:53.010
because, with your keen intuition,

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:56.680
you know there's nothing
left for you but defeat.

00:09:00.350 --> 00:09:02.020
That's Ri Boku for you.

00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:04.730
What an awful way to lower morale.

00:09:04.730 --> 00:09:06.230
Just awful!

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:09.440
Well...

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:13.950
I <i>will </i>say this one has
a hefty presence, yes.

00:09:13.950 --> 00:09:17.870
But Ou Ki was a man to be reckoned with.

00:09:17.870 --> 00:09:20.710
Why, isn't it rumored that he
would have bested even you,

00:09:20.710 --> 00:09:23.790
were it not for the arrow in his back?

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:28.380
The arrow matters not.

00:09:30.590 --> 00:09:34.890
Oho. He finally wavers, eh?

00:09:34.890 --> 00:09:38.770
Why are you here, Hou Ken?

00:09:38.770 --> 00:09:43.310
I heard you wouldn't have come to the
battlefield at all, if not for the history

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:45.310
you shared with Ou Ki.

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:50.990
Did you get lost chasing an illusion
of the Ou Ki you couldn't defeat?

00:09:57.080 --> 00:09:59.660
Do not get cocky.

00:09:59.660 --> 00:10:02.160
I am come

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:07.960
to know Ou Ki's strength,
being one who sought not the truth.

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:12.550
And did Ri Boku tell you the answer
lay on the battlefield?

00:10:15.090 --> 00:10:22.310
I see. Hou Ken, at last I've come
to understand you a little.

00:10:22.310 --> 00:10:24.020
Most likely,

00:10:26.060 --> 00:10:29.900
you're nothing but an imbecile
writhing in solitary agony,

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:33.860
unaware of the great
contradiction within you.

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:36.700
<i>What </i>did he say?

00:10:36.700 --> 00:10:38.030
No...

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:41.910
Lord Hyou has struck at the
very essence of Hou Ken.

00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:43.330
Hou Ken!

00:10:45.210 --> 00:10:48.670
Your answer is <i>indeed </i>
on the battlefield!

00:10:51.050 --> 00:10:53.300
Wh-What?!

00:10:53.300 --> 00:10:56.340
Lord Hyou is standing up to Hou Ken!

00:10:56.340 --> 00:10:57.760
Let's do our part, too!

00:10:57.760 --> 00:10:59.260
Slay Ri Boku!

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:02.600
Tch! They've found their second wind!

00:11:02.600 --> 00:11:05.390
Lord Hyou's formidable, all right.

00:11:05.390 --> 00:11:09.400
All main-unit troops,
take down Lord Hyou's men--now!

00:11:10.820 --> 00:11:13.190
Stay strong! Push on through!

00:11:13.190 --> 00:11:15.070
There's no use struggling!

00:11:16.990 --> 00:11:19.780
Apologies, but I can't allow
even the tiniest spark.

00:11:23.790 --> 00:11:25.120
Lieutenant Gaku Ga!

00:11:30.710 --> 00:11:33.340
My lord... may fortune be yours.

00:11:35.090 --> 00:11:37.800
You go on ahead and wait for me.

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:41.300
I'll be right there--bearing this one's
head as a present.

00:11:43.810 --> 00:11:44.810
Understood...

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:49.940
Yes! Soon Lord Hyou will be
the last one standing!

00:12:00.870 --> 00:12:01.830
Shin!

00:12:01.830 --> 00:12:04.200
Ri Boku's main unit--at last!

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:06.120
General Hyou!

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:14.000
Now, then...

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:16.130
General Hyou!

00:12:19.720 --> 00:12:23.510
Hang on, sir! We're comin' to help!

00:12:23.510 --> 00:12:25.220
Raise the flags!

00:12:25.220 --> 00:12:26.220
Sir!

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:29.900
My boy Shin!

00:12:29.900 --> 00:12:31.770
Shin, eh?

00:12:31.770 --> 00:12:33.690
It--it's just him!

00:12:33.690 --> 00:12:37.070
General Hyou's the only
one in their main unit!

00:12:37.070 --> 00:12:38.950
Say what?!

00:12:40.740 --> 00:12:43.160
Is another unit attempting to approach?

00:12:44.530 --> 00:12:47.660
It's not very big--not even
a hundred horses!

00:12:48.870 --> 00:12:50.920
General Hyou!

00:12:50.920 --> 00:12:53.420
General Hyou!

00:12:56.090 --> 00:12:58.380
You ain't goin' nowhere, moron!

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:05.810
Enough, Lord Hyou.

00:13:05.810 --> 00:13:10.020
Bringing in so few troops
won't change anything.

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:14.480
Shin, my boy!

00:13:17.230 --> 00:13:18.990
Onward!

00:13:22.240 --> 00:13:24.280
B-But where to?

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:25.580
Where is he pointing?

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:30.750
This is no place for
your flame to burn out!

00:13:30.750 --> 00:13:33.710
Shin, my boy, get yourself to Kanyou!

00:13:35.130 --> 00:13:36.250
To Kanyou?

00:13:39.050 --> 00:13:42.010
B-But that means he'll be...

00:13:43.430 --> 00:13:44.970
What the hell?!

00:13:44.970 --> 00:13:47.890
What's the big idea, General Hyou?

00:13:47.890 --> 00:13:49.850
General Hyou!

00:13:57.020 --> 00:13:59.820
H-His shield!

00:13:59.820 --> 00:14:02.030
That's General Hyou's shield!

00:14:04.820 --> 00:14:08.870
Now, then.
Sorry about the wait, Hou Ken.

00:14:08.870 --> 00:14:11.120
Let's finish this up, shall we?

00:14:12.250 --> 00:14:15.630
It is not that thou art
prepared for death.

00:14:15.630 --> 00:14:18.800
Thou hast given up on life.

00:14:18.800 --> 00:14:20.920
Thou art a weakling.

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:27.510
You understand nothing, you imbecile.

00:14:27.510 --> 00:14:33.270
You really don't feel a thing,
do you, Hou Ken.

00:14:33.270 --> 00:14:36.560
Not the strength that rises up within,

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:39.360
nor the flames that it spins into being!

00:14:39.360 --> 00:14:41.320
General!

00:14:41.320 --> 00:14:44.320
Which is why you weren't
able to defeat Ou Ki.

00:14:47.570 --> 00:14:51.790
I'll gladly give you your
answer in his stead:

00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:58.960
I'm not like Ou Ki and the others,
with their sweet battlefield dreams.

00:14:58.960 --> 00:15:02.380
I was born and raised on the battlefield.

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:07.140
My blade saw nothing but battle,
day in and day out.

00:15:07.140 --> 00:15:09.220
And compared to Ou Ki's,

00:15:09.220 --> 00:15:11.510
it's a damn sight more brutal!

00:15:55.270 --> 00:15:58.770
I'm taking your head with me, Hou Ken.

00:16:01.060 --> 00:16:04.320
Nearly dead--and with just one arm!

00:16:04.320 --> 00:16:08.490
That--that's what happened
with Ou Ki, too!

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:21.630
No--what he's <i>really </i>after...

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:27.670
Then this can be my consolation prize.

00:16:37.180 --> 00:16:38.730
Shin, my boy!

00:16:40.060 --> 00:16:43.110
Do <i>not </i>let your fire die out!

00:16:57.700 --> 00:17:01.250
I'm gonna be one of the
world's greatest generals!

00:17:01.250 --> 00:17:02.920
Shaddap!

00:17:02.920 --> 00:17:04.000
Oh, hey, yeah:

00:17:04.840 --> 00:17:10.090
There's somethin' I been meanin'
t' ask ya, General Hyou...

00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:11.970
What's that?

00:17:11.970 --> 00:17:17.140
How come you were never one
of the Six Great Generals?

00:17:17.140 --> 00:17:19.560
I mean, from where I stand,

00:17:19.560 --> 00:17:23.270
you're just as mighty as
Ou Ki and the rest.

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:28.900
That's an easy one.

00:17:28.900 --> 00:17:33.070
I just wasn't interested
in that kind of thing.

00:17:34.620 --> 00:17:37.870
Not <i>interested</i>?

00:17:37.870 --> 00:17:42.920
The way I see it, those fellows
were all dream-chasers,

00:17:42.920 --> 00:17:47.300
standing on the battlefield with their
minds set on some sweet dream.

00:17:47.300 --> 00:17:51.260
That resonated with the dreams of
King Sho, "the god of the battlefield,"

00:17:51.260 --> 00:17:54.930
to give off an intense power.

00:17:54.930 --> 00:17:58.100
But not me.

00:17:58.100 --> 00:18:02.890
I was born on the battlefield,
and there was I raised.

00:18:02.890 --> 00:18:04.230
Huh?

00:18:04.230 --> 00:18:10.240
The battlefield was my home,
and to fight was to live.

00:18:10.240 --> 00:18:14.910
In fact, King Sho summoned me
to Kanyou time and again,

00:18:14.910 --> 00:18:18.160
but I ignored his every request.

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:24.210
I didn't need the glorious radiance
or the dreams of the Six Greats.

00:18:24.210 --> 00:18:28.250
If I could but fight on the
battlefield, be victorious,

00:18:28.250 --> 00:18:30.510
and drink fine wine that evening,

00:18:30.510 --> 00:18:33.430
I would be satisfied.

00:18:33.430 --> 00:18:37.930
Satisfied with fine wine?
With all that might he has?

00:18:37.930 --> 00:18:41.850
Yeah, but that's cool in its own way.

00:18:41.850 --> 00:18:43.310
In other words,

00:18:43.310 --> 00:18:49.230
we were treading two
entirely different paths.

00:18:49.230 --> 00:18:53.780
B-But you and General Ou Ki
seemed pretty friendly.

00:18:53.780 --> 00:18:54.780
Oh?

00:18:55.610 --> 00:18:57.450
That's to be expected!

00:18:57.450 --> 00:18:59.490
This is the battlefield--

00:18:59.490 --> 00:19:02.620
what you're thinking hardly matters.

00:19:02.620 --> 00:19:05.120
What matters is how big
a flame you can kindle

00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:08.340
and how many foes you bury.

00:19:08.340 --> 00:19:14.130
Two mighty men will naturally be drawn
to one another, different paths or no.

00:19:16.260 --> 00:19:18.140
Now that I think of it,

00:19:18.140 --> 00:19:21.430
the wine we shared when I happened
to run into those fellows

00:19:21.430 --> 00:19:23.850
was <i>exceptionally </i>good.

00:19:30.730 --> 00:19:32.320
General Hyou.

00:19:32.320 --> 00:19:37.320
You're one helluva general,
at least as great as the Six Greats.

00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:39.070
Dakan Plain...

00:19:39.070 --> 00:19:42.200
I fought my first campaign
on your battlefield.

00:19:44.330 --> 00:19:46.370
At first, we pegged you for
some kinda crazy general

00:19:46.370 --> 00:19:49.210
who let his troops die left an' right!

00:19:49.210 --> 00:19:53.170
Right, Bi Hei, Taku--and Den Yuu!

00:19:53.170 --> 00:19:56.630
What?! Heck no, you idiot!
W-We would never!

00:19:58.720 --> 00:20:01.890
But I'm glad that's where I got my start.

00:20:01.890 --> 00:20:04.890
And I'm proud to be able
to fight beside you now

00:20:04.890 --> 00:20:08.310
and share a drink with you
like we're doin' tonight.

00:20:08.310 --> 00:20:11.820
So once I'm one of the
world's greatest generals,

00:20:11.820 --> 00:20:15.360
I'll serve you a way better
wine than what the Six--

00:20:17.150 --> 00:20:18.910
Uh, Shin? He's asleep.

00:20:18.910 --> 00:20:20.200
What?!

00:20:20.200 --> 00:20:21.780
Shin, my boy!

00:20:22.780 --> 00:20:28.620
We tread different paths,
but you just keep following yours.

00:20:28.620 --> 00:20:31.000
And one piece of advice:

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:33.710
The color of your flame isn't bad at all.

00:20:33.710 --> 00:20:38.970
But size-wise, it still cannot compare
to that of the Six Greats.

00:20:38.970 --> 00:20:42.470
'Course not! It's only gonna
get bigger from now on!

00:20:44.260 --> 00:20:47.560
Better wine than what
I drank with them, eh?

00:20:49.390 --> 00:20:52.980
I'm looking forward to that.

00:20:56.360 --> 00:20:58.530
General Hyou!

00:20:58.530 --> 00:21:02.070
General Hyou!

00:21:02.070 --> 00:21:03.150
You <i>bastards</i>!

00:21:03.150 --> 00:21:04.240
Shin, wait!

00:21:04.240 --> 00:21:04.950
Heki!

00:21:04.950 --> 00:21:07.620
General Hyou is already dead.

00:21:07.620 --> 00:21:11.460
He's <i>dead</i>, Shin!
There's no point going over there!

00:21:11.460 --> 00:21:13.750
What are you talking about, Heki?

00:21:13.750 --> 00:21:16.420
We'll avenge our general--

00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:18.760
that's where Ri Boku and Hou Ken are!

00:21:18.760 --> 00:21:20.220
How's <i>that </i>for a point?!

00:21:20.220 --> 00:21:23.640
We still couldn't kill them with
only a few dozen troops.

00:21:23.640 --> 00:21:26.180
Not even General Hyou
and his men could do it!

00:21:26.180 --> 00:21:28.770
If we head in there,
we'll be completely wiped out!

00:21:28.770 --> 00:21:32.440
Everyone would die, helpless--
and for what?

00:21:32.440 --> 00:21:34.310
You don't get to decide!

00:21:34.310 --> 00:21:36.400
Our general was killed
right before our eyes--

00:21:36.400 --> 00:21:39.240
and we just run away without
doin' what we gotta do?!

00:21:39.240 --> 00:21:41.950
I don't care <i>who </i>you are--
outta my way or I'll send you flyin'!

00:21:41.950 --> 00:21:44.910
Cool your head, you idiot!

00:21:44.910 --> 00:21:46.120
Shin!

00:21:46.120 --> 00:21:48.120
Captain Heki?

00:21:48.120 --> 00:21:52.330
Didn't you hear General Hyou say "Onward"?

00:21:52.330 --> 00:21:55.710
Don't you see what it means
that he tossed you his shield?

00:21:57.090 --> 00:22:01.300
If we don't get out of here
and respect his wishes--

00:22:01.300 --> 00:22:03.590
if we don't defend Kanyou--

00:22:03.590 --> 00:22:08.680
General Hyou's death itself
will lose all meaning, Shin!

00:22:16.110 --> 00:22:19.940
Under Heki's command,
Shin and the others escaped the flow.

00:22:19.940 --> 00:22:21.700
This way! Hurry!

00:22:24.240 --> 00:22:26.780
Stay on them! Keep attacking!

00:22:26.780 --> 00:22:29.620
Don't let them recover
and regroup at Kanyou!

00:22:42.720 --> 00:22:44.680
The captain! They made it!

00:22:44.680 --> 00:22:46.720
Shin!

00:22:46.720 --> 00:22:51.470
The troops separated by the Ryuudou
flow reunited on the outside,

00:22:51.470 --> 00:22:56.350
but the 5,000-troop Lord Hyou Army
was now down to 2,000.

00:22:56.350 --> 00:22:59.440
As the soldiers ran along the
southern path to Kanyou,

00:22:59.440 --> 00:23:03.400
attacks by pursuing Ri Boku troops
further thinned their ranks.

00:23:05.280 --> 00:23:07.700
Send word to Kanyou:

00:23:07.700 --> 00:23:10.990
"The general of this army is
Hou Ken of the Three Greats!

00:23:10.990 --> 00:23:14.000
A unit of elite forces from
our member nations

00:23:14.000 --> 00:23:16.750
has slain the Chin general Lord Hyou!"

00:23:16.750 --> 00:23:20.920
<i>That </i>is the greatest blow
we can deal Kanyou now!

00:24:52.510 --> 00:25:02.020
Sei's Decision

00:24:54.180 --> 00:24:57.930
Next on <i>Kingdom</i>: "Sei's Decision."
